:"rich_text","block_id":"blN"}]},{"client_msg_id":"e7fa38e5-9796-4f08-ba22-6e326f3e955f","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"C の挙動ってそこらへん明記されてましたっけ。自分は Go の挙動が自然に思えて、かつ C の大抵の処理系は同じ挙動をすると思っていました","ts":"1634821061.035100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Q4V"}]},{"client_msg_id":"06d1067b-ed2a-49fa-a395-b2cf34b4abfe","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"C言語的にはそんなもんだよなとは思ってたけど、goでそこらなんもケアした仕様じゃないんだなあと","ts":"1634821018.034300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Xy2k"}]},{"client_msg_id":"a1efb26d-afe9-41dd-8431-019ae831e763","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"uintの数値の最大値というべきでしたね、負数として上のサイズのものになるのではなく、そのサイズ内でそのまま補数処理されちゃうんだなと","ts":"1634820986.033600","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"5y9b"}]},{"client_msg_id":"19311cff-eb0d-4df5-96ce-1f618fda73f7","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"桁?","ts":"1634820874.031700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"M2Dv"}]},{"client_msg_id":"66e524d2-052e-4997-810c-0236e2b51fda","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"あー、まあそうなのか、桁が気になるけど、そこは自分でなんとかしろなのかな","ts":"1634820864.031300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"We9D"}]},{"client_msg_id":"A7591326-1268-4649-9EEE-86A532D66B8B","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"なるほど…","ts":"1634820789.030800","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"GKy"}]},{"client_msg_id":"74da51be-1e15-43f8-a627-b9a2115aa052","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"`-` をつけるのは `-1` を乗算するのとおなじ","ts":"1634820670.030500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ioh"}]},{"client_msg_id":"523F67B8-394F-4BF8-9638-3C27CA713B89","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"おー、そうなんですね。その辺曖昧なまま数値型触ってました…。低レイヤーこわい。","ts":"1634820668.030400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"pi5OX"}]},{"client_msg_id":"7174ca0f-25b0-4415-8a1d-22417b50330a","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"そうだと思います (int/uint は加算、減算、乗算については、ビット列の結果が全く同じはず)","ts":"1634820620.028700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"CUo"}]},{"client_msg_id":"FE8985AE-CF05-4128-B592-4CF4004D6EA3","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"あー、2の補数ですね。その辺の知識飛んでました。\nしかしそうすると結局、頭にマイナスつける演算子？はuintでもint扱いでビット演算するという挙動になるってことですかね。","ts":"1634820540.027600","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"sorena","count":1,"users":["U06BRP8VD"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"sTQ"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3b6fdda2-c7a4-4454-bb04-904d51b5ae35","type":"message","user":"U06BRP8VD","text":"\u0026gt; 符号反転した後に +1 かな\n2の補数 = 1の補数をとって+1\n\n\u003chttps://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/2%E3%81%AE%E8%A3%9C%E6%95%B0\u003e","ts":"1634819335.024900","attachments":[{"fallback":"wikipedia: 2の補数","id":1,"author_name":"Wikipedia","author_link":"https://ja.wikipedia.org/","title":"2の補数","title_link":"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/2%E3%81%AE%E8%A3%9C%E6%95%B0","text":"2の補数（にのほすう）は、2、ないし2のべき乗の補数、またそれによる負の値の表現法である。特に二進法で使われる。（数学的あるいは理論的には、三進法における減基数による補数、すなわち 3n − 1 ＝ 2222....2222(3) による補数も「2の補数」であるが、まず使われることはない）\nコンピュータの固定長整数型や、固定小数点数で、負の値を表現するためや加算器で減算をするために使われる。\n頭の部分の1個以上の0を含む（正規化されていない）ある桁数の二進法で表現された数があるとき、その最上位ビット (MSB) よりひとつ上のビットが1で、残りが全て0であるような値（8ビットの整数であれば、1000000002 = 256）から、元の数を引いた数が2の補数である。MSBの重みが1であるような固定小数点表現の場合は特に「2」の補数となる。","blocks":null,"service_icon":"https://a.slack-edge.com/80588/img/unfurl_icons/wikipedia.png","from_url":"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/2%E3%81%AE%E8%A3%9C%E6%95%B0","original_url":"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/2%E3%81%AE%E8%A3%9C%E6%95%B0"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"JMt+"}]},{"client_msg_id":"d5a59b44-5e8f-4693-afcd-1986894ca6bf","type":"message","user":"U06BRP8VD","text":"いや結論としては2の補数だな。 uint に対する `-` 演算が2の補数を求めるよう定義されてるんじゃなかろか。\n\n-1 を uint にした時点で 0xffff...ffff でしょ。\nそれに `-` を適用すると 0x0000...0001 になってるから。\n\n\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/rGqTB4uZQEi\u003e","ts":"1634819289.024300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"2to"}]},{"client_msg_id":"35bf40d0-30b3-4271-9ab7-0fac6f8a70a3","type":"message","user":"U06BRP8VD","text":"あ、問題設定間違ってるか。","ts":"1634818886.022500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"2IMNn"}]},{"client_msg_id":"87b0d483-6cb5-4b15-bed2-e7a5ae3a6393","type":"message","user":"U06BRP8VD","text":"たぶんそうじゃないかな。変数でやると期待通り2の補数だよ。\n\n\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/HpzTHC8Mgd-\u003e","ts":"1634818728.022300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"WrGks"}]},{"client_msg_id":"181d9441-9047-437e-9292-dd67e7b0f0c0","type":"message","user":"U06BRP8VD","text":"定数扱いで巻き取られている可能性は?","ts":"1634818584.021900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"IPhrh"}]},{"client_msg_id":"5489a753-1128-474f-a02a-3d8672325eb3","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"全然未定義動作じゃなかった…","ts":"1634818436.021300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"UQOq"}]},{"client_msg_id":"80d8bde3-fa03-48fc-a8d9-ec768be3503c","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"符号なし整数の加減のoverflowはwrapping aroundですね。uint64なら1\u0026lt;\u0026lt;64, uintなら1\u0026lt;\u0026lt;bits.UintSizeを法とする剰余演算になっている。i := uint64(10); println(-i == 1\u0026lt;\u0026lt;64 - 10) // true doc/specのInteger overflowが該当しそうな話。","ts":"1634818336.021000","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"eyes","count":1,"users":["U9S4G0LJW"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"7JoWL"}]},{"client_msg_id":"e5be60f2-8948-4045-a40f-1f5e7f595703","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"符号反転した後に +1 かな","ts":"1634817821.016900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"LnU"}]},{"client_msg_id":"63a742fb-692a-43ea-b7f3-749b7d7cc778","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/jCale4mLr8K\u003e 0 をかんがえると符号反転ではないですね","ts":"1634817807.016600","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Rahp"}]},{"client_msg_id":"d9ffcdc6-d1a5-4859-8dcd-a95aeb855e02","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/ZnAVS6hxBDA\u003e 逆もまた然り","ts":"1634817777.016400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"eHGz"}]},{"client_msg_id":"8fee201c-78a2-40d2-958a-9b073e6af4a9","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/5LyzPsOjFzL\u003e","ts":"1634817657.016200","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"RJYUJ"}]},{"client_msg_id":"35314a8a-775c-4c06-82d2-082f40571082","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"uint にキャストした後にマイナスか","ts":"1634817628.016000","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"7Bg"}]},{"client_msg_id":"4cb93959-391a-4749-bded-f53e139f695b","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/Im_PuufhYEr\u003e そうはなりませんでしたが…","ts":"1634817606.015400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"yCF"}]},{"client_msg_id":"20eed535-9e6e-434e-b47c-564fbedf5693","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"だねえ","ts":"1634816343.015200","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"d1y"}]},{"client_msg_id":"822eb327-3851-432b-a824-9aed0e2c5177","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"でもuintで符号ビット反転できるのは違和感ありますね・・・。","ts":"1634815994.013900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"y8aAO"}]},{"client_msg_id":"13dab5d6-6960-4e3d-b66d-f6122de869c2","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"-を頭につけるのは符号反転みたいですが、ひょっとしてuintに適用する場合は（intの場合の）符号ビット位置のビットを反転するという挙動になるんですかね。それだと説明がつくのですが。","ts":"1634815970.013400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Ao=Wp"}]},{"client_msg_id":"5adc5c09-c139-4346-9396-15ed2bb9cf9b","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"あー","ts":"1634815458.011900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"X9pu"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3a590792-8b8e-4705-a208-00132454af14","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"という記述しか見付けられなかった","ts":"1634815443.011600","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"C7Lnw"}]},{"client_msg_id":"11d63a46-0b4b-4a41-8b2e-b5d402584a2a","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"\u0026gt; uint(-1)     // -1 cannot be represented as a uint","ts":"1634815429.011100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"oQ2"}]},{"client_msg_id":"8215205e-1224-4ec2-be7c-0df99c257b36","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"specざっと眺めてみたけど未定義動作みがある","ts":"1634815388.010900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"2wm"}]},{"client_msg_id":"bb000cf4-0d25-46c2-93e2-632c6296dabb","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"キャストが「uintへの意味的な変換」ではなく「uintへのデータ上の変換」で負数が巨大な正の数になり\nそしてそれに負の符号を付けた状態で暗黙のキャストがされる uint への代入をしたことでこうなった、かなあ?","ts":"1634815186.010400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"b/Y"}]},{"client_msg_id":"50bd2a36-3862-4ed3-b021-3f800598ff89","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"まあキャストするのはプログラマの責任なのでしょうがないのですが・・・。\n負の値をuintにキャストしたあとにマイナスつけてるコードをたまたま見かけて、実際に結果の値は合っていたのでなんでだろうなーと思いまして。","ts":"1634815029.008700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"/CHF"}]},{"client_msg_id":"26103a53-c2d1-46c0-b1a7-d776d1247f0d","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"むうん、どうなんでしょうね\nというかz uintに 負数をブチ込めちゃうのもどうなんでしょうね...","ts":"1634814472.005800","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ahG"}]},{"client_msg_id":"04e20603-8818-4e24-8e31-d147d4765b26","type":"message","user":"U023Z8L90BG","text":"負の値のint型変数をuintにキャストした後に-をつけると元の値を符号反転した値になるのですがこの挙動についての説明ってどこかにあったりしますでしょうか？\nint -\u0026gt; uint で大きな値になるのは符号bitがそのまま数値になっているんだと思うのですが、マイナスをつけるとintを反転した値になる理屈がよく分からず。\n\u003chttps://play.golang.org/p/Q_RRNXtK1cM\u003e","ts":"1634814360.005100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"aTBKL"}]},{"client_msg_id":"4609556F-1206-4EA6-A858-95FA6C58AC3F","type":"message","user":"U7H4TJEG0","text":"\u003chttps://golang.org/cl/357330|https://golang.org/cl/357330\u003e これは期待。インタープリター速くなりそう。","ts":"1634747482.442900","attachments":[{"fallback":"Gerrit Code Review","id":1,"text":"Gerrit Code Review","blocks":null,"service_name":"go-review.googlesource.com","service_icon":"https://go-review.googlesource.com/favicon.ico","from_url":"https://golang.org/cl/357330","original_url":"https://golang.org/cl/357330"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ZxNy"}]},{"client_msg_id":"ba2b0414-73e5-42e4-a3b3-4772179a2c4e","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"(さっきの意味文脈ではuintはあっていいけど数値としてbyteから変換してあとは普通に数値処理できたらなあ、みたいなのがありました、uintがあるのはいいんですよ....)","ts":"1634824562.078500","thread_ts":"1634824504.077500","parent_user_id":"U01JDE048LA","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"IqHU"}]},{"client_msg_id":"f02086f3-c86d-4f71-8a0c-8ca055cd7216","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"とフォローというか言い訳","ts":"1634824572.078700","thread_ts":"1634824504.077500","parent_user_id":"U01JDE048LA","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"U30s"}]},{"client_msg_id":"9d642a05-7b3a-43a8-a2a4-5b5096d25eb9","type":"message","user":"U01JDE048LA","text":"それは、Rob Pike も こんな提案しているので、やりたいというのはあるんじゃないでしょうか？ \u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/19623\u003e","ts":"1634825436.079000","thread_ts":"1634824504.077500","attachments":[{"color":"36a64f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/19623|#19623 proposal: spec: change int to be arbitrary precision\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/19623|#19623 proposal: spec: change int to be arbitrary precision\u003e","text":"An idea that has been kicking around for years, but never written down:\n\nThe current definition of `int` (and correspondingly `uint`) is that it is either 32 or 64 bits. This causes a variety of problems that are small but annoying and add up:\n\n• overflow when constants like math.MaxUint64 is automatically promoted to `int` type\n• maximum size of a byte slice is only half the address space on a 32-bit machine\n• `int` values can overflow silently, yet no one depends on this working. (Those who want overflow use sized types.)\n• great care must be taken with conversion between potentially large values, as information can be lost silently\n• many more\n\nI propose that for Go 2 we make a profound change to the language and have `int` and `uint` be arbitrary precision. It can be done efficiently - many other languages have done so - and with the new compiler it should be possible to avoid the overhead completely in many cases. (The usual solution is to represent an integer as a word with one bit reserved; for instance if clear, the word points to a \u003chttp://big.Int|big.Int\u003e or equivalent, while if set the bit is just cleared or shifted out.)\n\nThe advantages are many:\n\n• `int` (and `uint`, but I'll stop mentioning it now) become very powerful types\n• overflow becomes impossible, simplifying and securing many calculations\n• the default type for `len` etc. can now capture any size without overflow\n• we could permit any integer type to be converted to `int` without ceremony, simplifying some arithmetical calculations\n\nMost important, I think it makes Go a lot more interesting. No language in its domain has this feature, and the advantages of security and simplicity it would bring are significant.","fields":[{"title":"Labels","value":"LanguageChange, Go2, Proposal, NeedsInvestigation","short":true},{"title":"Comments","value":"115","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go|golang/go\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1490039379}],"parent_user_id":"U01JDE048LA","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ge59"}]},{"client_msg_id":"4b883747-6beb-4a21-b231-8ae897521ec4","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"ほー","ts":"1634825606.079300","thread_ts":"1634824504.077500","parent_user_id":"U01JDE048LA","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"5RVC"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3a6c761b-40eb-42e4-860d-f33d7991ce13","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"CLS (Common Language Specification) でした","ts":"1634824215.073900","thread_ts":"1634823998.071700","parent_user_id":"UERCTTT8B","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"A=LdR"}]},{"client_msg_id":"9e005239-9d63-464b-906c-0aa703508247","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"C# に uint はあるけど、つかうと CLS compliant ではなくなる","ts":"1634824230.074100","thread_ts":"1634823998.071700","parent_user_id":"UERCTTT8B","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"aY0"}]},{"client_msg_id":"55457d6a-ddf3-4612-82b5-4e4b6ee134af","type":"message","user":"UAZ33BKV2","text":"へー、つかうとあかん型があるのびっくり\nネイティブ対応用?","ts":"1634824354.074400","thread_ts":"1634823998.071700","parent_user_id":"UERCTTT8B","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"0lel"}]},{"client_msg_id":"c5e2f27c-6a65-44dc-8984-8bbc8ef3f0aa","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"他の言語 (\u003chttp://VB.NET|VB.NET\u003e とか) と連携するときにつかってはいけない型ですね","ts":"1634824392.074600","thread_ts":"1634823998.071700","edited":{"user":"UERCTTT8B","ts":"1634824429.000000"},"parent_user_id":"UERCTTT8B","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"FBgk"}]},{"client_msg_id":"5a0236f2-6152-4c8d-ab6e-bf193ecbf55c","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"そして事実上 .NET は C# 一択なのであんまり意味が…ない…","ts":"1634824414.075300","thread_ts":"1634823998.071700","parent_user_id":"UERCTTT8B","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"jt8"}]}]
